                  1oo% C/OFF,v1.0b (20-Feb-97) by Adolescent
                    ANSI/cursor LogOFF Matrix for CNet BBS


Info:
            ANSi/cursor Logoff Matrix for CNet/3                      
            (displays a configurable menu of pre-logoff activities...)


Note:       This program should work on CNet/4 but hasn't been tested. If
            you have _ANY_ problems with it please let me know and I will
            fix it ASAP and send it to you...  (I took out a high getuser
            that has been known to 'shift' in the beta versions.)


Features:
            -  ONline CONFIG ED (see below for needed instructions...)
            -  Configable COLORS/APPEARANCE
            -  ANSI/COLOR/CURSOR/etc...
            -  Replaces _ALL_ Off, O!, Relogon, Quit, etc. functions.

Install:
            1) Copy LOGOFF.REXX to PFiles:1oo/LOGOFF/   (or wherever)
            
            2) Copy ???.LOGOFF to SYSTEXT:

            3) Load BBSMENU in your fave text editor and change these... 
               (please note that MOST have tilde '~' VERY IMPORTANT!!!
               
               3; Main prompt
                  Relogon               |{#0Pfiles:1oo/LOGOFF/LOGOFF.rexx}
                  Quit,Off,LOGOFF       |{#0Pfiles:1oo/LOGOFF/LOGOFF.rexx}~

               4; ud/base 
                  Off,LOGOFF            |{#0Pfiles:1oo/LOGOFF/LOGOFF.rexx}~

               6; News/Gfiles/Pfiles
                  Off,LOGOFF            |{#0Pfiles:1oo/LOGOFF/LOGOFF.rexx}~


              14; Bbslist
                  Off,LOGOFF            |{#0Pfiles:1oo/LOGOFF/LOGOFF.rexx}~


            4) ReLOAD BBSTEXT/BBSMENU and type OFF to test/configure.

      (OPT) 5) Load LOGOFF.REXX into a text editor and change colors...
      
      (OPT) 6) Edit ???.LOGOFF files to suit your BBS style...


Online editor:

            Access the online config by pressing the 'C' key when cOFF is    
            running.(edit MIN in the LOGOFF.REXX file to your preference)
            (note:  the paths, files, etc. in these examples may vary...)


           *To ADD an item:

            1) Choose a number higher than the last number listed.

            2) Enter the item name as you would like it to be displayed
               on the matrix.  (max 20 characters)
        
               ex.  BBSlist  

            3) Enter the full MCI (minus the brackets) of the file you 
               would like to run, display, etc...  (max 40 characters)                        

               ex.  #2PFILES:BBSLIST 

            4) Choose a witty description line. (max 70 characters)

               ex.  Find a better place to call

            5) Choose 'S' to save.

            
           *To EDIT an item:

            1) Type a number from the list.

            2) Follow instructions, if no change, press enter.

            3) Choose 'S' to save.


           *To DELETE an item:

            1) Press 'D'
        
            2) Choose number to delete.

            3) Choose 'S' to save.
              

Bugs:
            None!  (that I know of!)  This file has been tested on my BBS
            for about 9-10 months with no problems.  If you find any send
            me email at the address below.


